cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite HINC-001 as a public-review candidate package. Cite a later DOI or
  archival release if one becomes available.
title: Hidden Infinitesimal Noncommutativity in Endomorphism Monoids of Two Graded Gerstenhaber Algebras
type: article
version: 0.1.0-public-review
date-released: 2026-07-27
authors:
  - family-names: Novak
    given-names: Matthew S.
abstract: >-
  We give a self-contained candidate classification of strict graded
  Gerstenhaber endomorphism monoid schemes for two explicit
  characteristic-two subalgebras of the Hochschild cohomology of the dual
  numbers. The two monoids share a reduced crossing core but differ by an
  infinitesimal skew thickening and a clopen unit doubling. A bounded
  algebraic kernel and the principal coefficient classifications are publicly
  proof-assistant verified; the complete scheme-level manuscript remains
  under specialist and historical-equivalence review. ChatGPT materially
  assisted the research under human direction; OpenAI did not sponsor,
  review, approve, or endorse the work.
repository-code: https://github.com/novakprotocol/N-Human-AI-Mathematics
keywords:
  - algebraic monoids
  - Gerstenhaber algebra
  - Hochschild cohomology
  - nonreduced schemes
  - formal verification
  - human-AI mathematics
  - ChatGPT-assisted research
